From: Folklore port <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 0008] Per-thread guest callback stacks; AIO latency; diagnostics

1. ppu_guest_call / ppu_guest_call_ct: each host thread gets its own 64 KB
   callback stack from the PPU stack region (on first use), instead of one
   scratch stack at 0xCFFE0000 shared by every host thread -- a callback on a
   game thread (cellVdec PICOUT) and one on the vblank ticker (GCM flip
   handler) could run on the same guest stack at once. Callbacks also inherit
   the calling thread's TLS (r13). PS3_CB_SCRATCH_STACK=1 restores the old
   stack.
2. cellFsAioRead completions arrive after 25 ms (PS3_FS_AIO_LATENCY_MS), like
   a disc read; PS3_FS_AIO_SUBMIT_DELAY_MS (default 0) for experiments.
3. Diagnostics: PS3_CONDLOG=1 logs sys_cond_wait calls, PS3_CONDLOG_SIGNAL=<id>
   the signals of one cond; cellVdec logs the callback's return value (first
   three per message type, and every non-zero one).

diff --git a/libs/codec/cellVdec.c b/libs/codec/cellVdec.c
index 4f3f3ce..e129ed2 100644
--- a/libs/codec/cellVdec.c
+++ b/libs/codec/cellVdec.c
@@ -78,8 +78,20 @@ static void vdec_notify(CellVdecHandle handle, u32 msg_type, s32 msg_data)
     if (handle >= MAX_VDEC || !s_vdec[handle].in_use) return;
     const VdecSlot* v = &s_vdec[handle];
     if (!v->cbFunc || !g_ps3_guest_caller) return;
-    g_ps3_guest_caller(v->cbFunc, (u64)handle, (u64)msg_type,
-                       (u64)(s64)msg_data, (u64)v->cbArg, 0, 0, 0, 0);
+    /* The callback's return value says whether the title accepted the
+     * message; log the first few of each type and every non-zero one. */
+    extern u64 ppu_guest_call(u32 opd, u64 a0, u64 a1, u64 a2, u64 a3,
+                              u64 a4, u64 a5, u64 a6, u64 a7);
+    u64 rc = ppu_guest_call(v->cbFunc, (u64)handle, (u64)msg_type,
+                            (u64)(s64)msg_data, (u64)v->cbArg, 0, 0, 0, 0);
+    { static u32 s_seen[4]; static u32 s_bad;
+      u32 slot = msg_type < 4 ? msg_type : 3;
+      if (s_seen[slot] < 3 || (rc && s_bad < 16)) {
+          if (rc) s_bad++;
+          s_seen[slot]++;
+          fprintf(stderr, "[cellVdec] callback(msg=%u data=0x%X) -> 0x%llX\n",
+                  msg_type, (u32)msg_data, (unsigned long long)rc);
+      } }
 }
 
